[contract-gate] Anchor contract gate (complete)
Files: spec/initial.md; roadmap.md; proposals/semantic-contract.md; proposals/cellular-automata-anchor.md; proposals/discontinuity-projection.md
Do: Keep the empty-journal anchor rule canonical, remove stale fold language, make unsupported CreateSaucer radii explicit failures, and keep the piece contract honest about query-local rule calculation over immutable piece inputs.
Accept: Canonical spec, roadmap, proposals, and public query/error behavior agree; no malformed radius is silently ignored.
> Decision: LogicalTime and Tau use signed i64 milliseconds (1,000 ticks per logical second); the automaton game tick remains one logical second.
> Anchor game tick period is one second of logical time; LogicalTime/Tau may use finer fixed-point resolution independently of the game tick.
> An entry is visible at its exact timestamp. A journal entry inside a game tick participates in automaton behavior at the next tick boundary; an entry exactly on a tick boundary participates in that tick.
> Empty-journal and pre-CreateSaucer queries use the ordinary zero-fact/default path and return the empty set; CreateSaucer at t_=0 adds the 91-tile saucer.
> A postdated entry may be authored into the immutable journal before evaluation; queries ignore entries after their requested t_.
> Acts, moves, destroys, ignites, and converts are indexed differences between returned values, never mutation or actor execution.
> ReferenceContext carries the anchor radius definition only; a visible CreateSaucer entry materializes the instance saucer.
> At one activation tick on one tile, authored SetTerrain entries precede derived terrain events by journal append order; derived events use the fixed anchor rule order and stable actor/tile order.
> Unsupported visible CreateSaucer radii are explicit ProjectionError values on try_state and invalid persistence records.
---
[discontinuity-contract] Discontinuity and piecewise contract (complete)
Do: Keep immutable half-open selection generic while making Caravan piece payloads carry immutable visible journal inputs and a projection regime. Document query-local rule calculation, same-tick terrain precedence, and collective live actor occupancy.
Accept: Selected pieces expose their immutable visible inputs; the proposal does not claim callable projection functions are stored in generic pieces.
-> contract-gate
> Indexed pieces are half-open intervals [start_t,end_t).
> Exact journal timestamps and game-tick boundaries remain distinct discontinuities; entries inside a tick affect the next tick-boundary behavior, while entries on a tick boundary participate in that tick.
> The discontinuity index is an immutable derived value built from immutable worldline and journal inputs.
> Breakpoint and piece selection is generic and engine-neutral; the engine does not own Caravan game primitives.
> Caravan owns definition-specific thresholds and visibility rules, including actor, fire, and resource thresholds.
> Same-tick terrain precedence is Caravan-owned: authored SetTerrain entries retain journal append order and precede derived terrain events on the same tile; derived events retain fixed source and actor/tile order.
> The selected Caravan piece owns immutable visible journal inputs and a projection regime; rule calculation remains query-local.
> The actor layer uses shared live occupancy across transitions, including spawn visibility, removals, movement, conflicts, and collisions.
@guidance text/markdown proposals/discontinuity-projection.md
